<h2>Usage</h2>
<h3>Guidance</h3>
<div class="nsw-grid nsw-m-top-sm">
  <div class="nsw-col nsw-col-sm-6 nsw-docs__guideline">
    <div class="nsw-docs__guideline--do"><span class="material-icons nsw-material-icons" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">check_circle</span><span>Do</span></div>
    <ul class="nsw-m-top-sm">
      <li>use steps to draw a connection for the user between linear pieces of information</li>
      <li>use steps for steps or stages of a process</li>
      <li>use steps for sequential dates or outcomes.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="nsw-col nsw-col-sm-6 nsw-docs__guideline">
    <div class="nsw-docs__guideline--dont"><span class="material-icons nsw-material-icons" focusable="false" aria-hidden="true">cancel</span><span>Don't</span></div>
    <ul class="nsw-m-top-sm">
      <li>use steps when content doesn't come together in sequential or linear order; consider bullet points instead.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Step types</h2>
<p>Steps use colours from your brand palette, displayed as outlined or filled. Counters can also be added where they correspond to the content. Colour selection should take into considertation the contrast with the content background.</p>
<p>Based on your heading class, small and medium sized steps are available to ensure the component remains visually balance. </p>


<h2>Accessibility</h2>
<p>All components are responsive and designed to comply with WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility standards. Full compliance depends on using and configuring the components correctly.</p>
